# CompactList row affordances (review-only, no goldens): a device page whose rows carry each kind (Edit: value in its
# tone then the chevron; Open: the chevron; Info: no chevron, a Normal value grey, an explicit Bad value still red;
# Action: a white dot in the chevron's slot, the label white; Action running: the dot in the accent blue; one
# Unspecified row as today), in both densities, each kind on a plain row and on the selected one (the #2B2B2B bar, bold
# label). expect_chevron checks the chevron (grey, drawn, right of the texts, inside the row, centred on its middle,
# larger than the label, row height unchanged); expect_dot the dot (its colour drawn, a circle of the list's dot size,
# centred on the row's middle and in the chevron's slot, the value ending in the chevron rows' column); expect_color the
# colours. The dot switches between idle and running through the live refresh (set_rows: setkind) and update_row (kind)
# without a rebuild: switched back, the screen is pixel-identical to the shot before (expect_same; a rebuild would move
# the selection and the scroll). Then the legacy case: an untagged list tagged with five kinds and set back to
# Unspecified is pixel-identical to the shot taken before.
title compact list row affordances
review
sizes 640x480 800x480 480x320 720x720 1280x720
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
# --- Comfortable: row 0 (Edit) selected
listdemo comfortable 11 kinds
expect_color "Automatic (wlan0)" 00CC66
expect_chevron Network yes
expect_dot Network no
expect_chevron "Diagnose my connection" yes
expect_color "Diagnose my connection" FFFFFF
expect_color 02:00:00:00:00:01 9A9A9A
expect_chevron "MAC address" no
expect_dot "MAC address" no
expect_color "MAC address" FFFFFF
expect_color "2 ms" 9A9A9A
expect_color Down FF6666
shot aff_comfortable_top
# Open selected, Edit plain
key DOWN
expect_chevron "Diagnose my connection" yes
expect_chevron Network yes
expect_color "Automatic (wlan0)" 00CC66
# Info selected
key DOWN
expect_color 02:00:00:00:00:01 9A9A9A
expect_chevron "MAC address" no
# Info with an explicit Bad tone, selected: the tone wins
key DOWN
key DOWN
expect_color Down FF6666
expect_chevron Link no
expect_dot Link no
# Action (idle) selected: white label, white dot
key DOWN
key DOWN
expect_color "Save for Wake-on-LAN" FFFFFF
expect_chevron "Save for Wake-on-LAN" no
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
expect_dot "Ping this device" no
shot aff_comfortable_action
# Action (idle) plain
key DOWN
expect_color /dev/ttyUSB0 00CC66
expect_chevron Port no
expect_dot Port no
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
expect_color "Save for Wake-on-LAN" FFFFFF
expect_chevron "Ping this device" yes
shot aff_comfortable_port
# the action starts (live refresh, set_rows): the plain row's dot turns blue, nothing else moves; it stops: as before
listdemo setkind 6 action-running
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" running
expect_color "Save for Wake-on-LAN" FFFFFF
shot aff_comfortable_running_plain
listdemo setkind 6 action
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
expect_same aff_comfortable_port
# the end: an action running with a value, selected (its value in the chevron rows' column)
key END
expect_dot Listen running
expect_color Listen FFFFFF
expect_color listening 00CC66
expect_chevron Listen no
shot aff_comfortable_end
# a long label cut before its chevron, a long value whole before its chevron (the label "Server" gives way: cut with
# dots, so the row is found by its value); the running action below it, plain
key UP
expect_chevron build-server.home.arpa yes
expect_text build-server.home.arpa
expect_dot Listen running
# update_row on the selected running row: idle, then running again
key DOWN
listdemo kind 10 action
expect_dot Listen idle
shot aff_comfortable_idle_selected
listdemo kind 10 action-running
expect_dot Listen running
expect_same aff_comfortable_end
# --- Compact (a section first): row 1 (Edit) selected
listdemo compact 12 kinds
expect_chevron Network yes
expect_color "Automatic (wlan0)" 00CC66
expect_chevron "Diagnose my connection" yes
expect_color 02:00:00:00:00:01 9A9A9A
expect_chevron "MAC address" no
expect_color Down FF6666
expect_chevron "Ping this device" yes
expect_chevron "Save for Wake-on-LAN" no
shot aff_compact_top
# Action (idle) selected
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
expect_color "Save for Wake-on-LAN" FFFFFF
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
expect_chevron "Ping this device" yes
shot aff_compact_action
# Open selected, Action (idle) plain, then running plain (live refresh), then running selected
key UP
expect_chevron "Ping this device" yes
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
listdemo setkind 7 action-running
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" running
key DOWN
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" running
expect_color "Save for Wake-on-LAN" FFFFFF
shot aff_compact_running
listdemo setkind 7 action
expect_dot "Save for Wake-on-LAN" idle
expect_same aff_compact_action
key DOWN
expect_chevron Port no
expect_dot Port no
expect_color /dev/ttyUSB0 00CC66
key END
expect_dot Listen running
expect_color listening 00CC66
shot aff_compact_end
key UP
expect_chevron build-server.home.arpa yes
expect_text build-server.home.arpa
expect_dot Listen running
# --- Legacy: the untagged 12-row menu, tagged, then back to Unspecified: pixel-identical
listdemo comfortable 12
wait 1500
shot aff_legacy
expect_chevron Port no
expect_dot Port no
expect_color /dev/ttyUSB0 00CC66
listdemo kind 0 edit
expect_chevron Port yes
expect_color /dev/ttyUSB0 00CC66
listdemo kind 1 action
expect_color "Baud rate" FFFFFF
expect_dot "Baud rate" idle
listdemo kind 2 info
expect_color 8 9A9A9A
listdemo kind 3 open
expect_chevron Parity yes
listdemo kind 4 action-running
expect_dot "Stop bits" running
shot aff_legacy_tagged
listdemo kind 0 unspecified
listdemo kind 1 unspecified
listdemo kind 2 unspecified
listdemo kind 3 unspecified
listdemo kind 4 unspecified
expect_chevron Port no
expect_chevron Parity no
expect_dot "Baud rate" no
expect_dot "Stop bits" no
expect_color "Baud rate" FFFFFF
expect_color 8 00CC66
expect_same aff_legacy
